# Compact smooth graph approximation: independent source preread

Owner: phase_source_reviewer_20261005; 2026-10-06.
Inspected committed HEAD: `30ad6ddb991c190d912d5bd8a48b39bd486d4d7b`.
This is a bounded source/API prerequisite audit. No candidate source verdict,
compilation, mathematical admission or lifecycle change is recorded.

## Source boundary reconstructed before the proposal

[PBPS arXiv:2609.06905v1 Section2.2](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#S2.SS2),
HTML168–211, equations2.6–2.14, supplies the normalized Gibbs/Gaussian augmentation.
[Appendix C.1](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1),
HTML1197–1234 and1276–1310, uses smooth compact tests, gradient closedness/density,
and H1 approximation; its conditional integration-by-parts identity and
continuity of covariance require separate arguments. It does not state a
Laplacian graph-core theorem.

The true reflected conditional potential is
\[
 W^S_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+\|z-y\|^2/(8\eta),
\]
whereas the ordinary RGO potential is
\(W^R_y(x)=V(x)+\|x-y\|^2/(2\eta)\).
Reflection \(z=2x-y\) has inverse Jacobian \(2^{-d}\) and quarter Hessian;
the corresponding unreflected Dirichlet energy is four times the reflected
energy. These require actual adapters, not identification of laws/operators.
[SPHMC arXiv:2609.06906v1 Section4.1](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.SS1),
HTML403–430, equation4.1/Lemma4.1, separately needs the RGO covariance bounds.
This proposed approximation edge is an authored analytic prerequisite, not a
numbered source theorem, conditional Poincare, BL or a main result.

## Exact seven-slot contract for the proposed bounded edge

- **Objects:** same actual resolvent solution u and G=D.closure(u); for each real
  C2 compact chi, actual v=chi*u, g=chi*G+u*gradient(chi), and
  F=chi*r+2 inner(gradient(chi),G)+u*Delta(chi), with
  r=epsilon*u+inner(gradient(W),G)-f. Current outputs include genuine ordinary
  global volume-L2 of all three, their support inclusions, all-C1 weak gradient,
  all-C2 weak PDE, and actual complex vc/Fc AE ofReal(v/F), Delta(Tvc)=TFc,
  MemSobolev2(Tvc). Different representatives/classes must keep these AE links.
- **Domains:** finite real Hilbert/Borel space with canonical ordinary volume,
  including dimension zero. D is the original densely defined compact-smooth
  gradient in weighted L2(S_y), not a newly substituted operator. The new sequence
  consists of real C-infinity functions on the entire space with compact support.
  Convergence is ordinary-volume L2, not merely pointwise, local L2 or weighted L2.
- **Quantifiers:** common R/S, then every y and one original D_y, then every
  epsilon>0/forcing f, then ONE u, then ALL real C2 compact chi. For each chi,
  choose one outer compact K' and one sequence phi_n before ALL n and ALL three
  limits. Each phi_n is smooth and supported in K'. The support need not equal
  tsupport(chi). A geometric K' can be chosen from chi alone; no measurable
  y-dependent solution/sequence selector is claimed.
- **Assumptions:** actual conditional C2 V, positive alpha<=beta, all-point/all-vector
  curvature, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1 remain unchanged. Positive integrable partitions,
  genuine kernels and exact original compact-smooth graph are derived parents.
  The shared edge may consume the actual localized global L2/support/weak
  equations and derived Sobolev output. It must not assume graph density, a smooth
  approximation sequence, real mixed derivatives or final weighted core membership.
- **Conclusion:** every phi_n, gradient(phi_n) and Delta(phi_n) is genuinely
  ordinary-volume MemLp2. Their actual Lp classes converge respectively to the
  classes of v, g and F, or equivalently their finite eLpNorm2 errors tend to zero
  with correct AE linkage. One sequence realizes all three limits and common
  support. Gradients/Laplacians are classical derivatives only of smooth phi_n;
  rough u/v retain weak/distribution meanings.
- **Scope:** this is compact ordinary-volume function/gradient/Laplacian graph
  approximation of the actual localized solution. Original weighted-domain
  membership, adjoint/operator-core identification, unlocalized cutoff removal,
  global Bochner, epsilon-zero, BL/Poincare, fiberwise measurable selection and
  both main results require further proofs. Directionwise real mixed-second
  representatives are not needed just to reach these three limits.
- **Constants:** preserve B2=I-(2*pi)^(-2)Delta. Inverse-Bessel symbols are
  m0=(1+norm(xi)^2)^(-1),
  mb=2*pi*i*inner(xi,b)/(1+norm(xi)^2),
  mDelta=-(2*pi)^2*norm(xi)^2/(1+norm(xi)^2).
  Bounds1,2*pi*norm(b),(2*pi)^2 suffice. No new dimension-free quantitative
  estimate is claimed; finite-basis assembly is only an existence/convergence step.

## Independent source-to-API route, at most seven steps

1. Use the actual Bessel witness w=vc-(2*pi)^(-2)Fc (or identify an existential
   witness with it using the actual TD PDE). Approximating vc in plain L2 would
   not control its gradient or Laplacian. Preserve every AE cast and measure.
2. Construct fixed-symbol continuous L2 maps M_m=FourierInv o multiply(m) o
   Fourier. This is a missing adapter, not supplied by Sobolev membership alone.
   Pinned Holder infinity,2,2 bounds and genuine Plancherel yield norm continuity.
   Prove compatibility with actual Schwartz and TD multipliers, including
   temperate growth, finite norm and chosen quotient representatives.
3. Actual Schwartz density in L2 produces a sequence q_n converging to w.
   Set s_n=FM(m0)q_n. The same sequence controls function, each finite-basis
   directional derivative and Laplacian via the bounded symbols. Inverse Bessel,
   actual Delta(Tvc)=TFc and Lp-TD injectivity identify the function/Laplacian
   limits with vc/Fc; no normalization factor is lost.
4. Identify each real directional-gradient limit with inner(g,b), using the
   original compact-C1 weak identity, smooth compact test IBP, continuity of
   Holder L2 pairings and compact-test uniqueness. Legal complex L1 precedes
   integral Re. Real-linear projection gives genuine real L2 limits; finite
   orthonormal-basis reconstruction yields convergence of the full gradient.
   This proves the actual g limit, not a newly chosen abstract gradient. No
   assumed all-Schwartz first-gradient identity or imaginary-zero certificate.
5. Choose a fixed smooth compact plateau theta=1 on a neighborhood of
   K=tsupport(chi), and put phi_n=theta*Re(s_n). Common K'=tsupport(theta)
   works for every n. Smooth product formulas give
   gradient(phi_n)=theta*gradient(Re(s_n))+Re(s_n)*gradient(theta) and
   Delta(phi_n)=theta*Delta(Re(s_n))+2 inner(gradient(theta),gradient(Re(s_n)))
   +Re(s_n)*Delta(theta). Fixed coefficients are bounded. Derivatives of theta
   vanish on K; actual v/g/F vanish off K. Thus all limiting cross terms vanish.
6. Prove MemLp2 of all actual approximants and product-rule terms before
   converting error estimates into actual quotient convergence. No division by
   dimension or a nonzero basis vector is permitted. In zero dimension the
   gradient/Laplacian vanish, B2=I, the basis is empty and the plateau is locally1
   at the sole point; canonical zero-dimensional volume remains the measure.
7. Reattach the sequence after each chi to the same original D/u and retain
   every prior conjunction. Stop at the ordinary compact graph. On this common
   compact support, later weighted transfer can use actual positive Z and local
   bounded density/gradient(W), but requires explicit quotient/AE adapters and
   original graph/closure reasoning. That extension is not part of this target.

## API proposal assessment and hidden analytic obligations

The read proposal `Weighted_compact_Sobolev_smooth_core_route_audit.md` was opened
only after fresh primary-source reconstruction, and is treated as an API plan,
not a proof certificate or source-fidelity verdict. Its spectral route is
consistent with the scoped three-limit target. Its later weighted-transfer/core
steps remain later consumers, rather than assumptions or conclusions of this edge.

Freshly inspected pinned Mathlib (`db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d`):
`SchwartzMap.denseRange_toLpCLM` (SchwartzSpace/Basic:1383–1395) gives actual
finite-p density; `Lp.fourierTransformₗᵢ`,
`norm_fourier_eq`, Schwartz Fourier/inverse compatibility and actual L2/TD
Fourier compatibility (Fourier/LpSpace:50–138) provide isometries and continuity.
`Lp.coeFn_lpSMul`/`Lp.norm_smul_le` (Holder:183–193) retain AE products and norms;
`Lp.toTemperedDistribution_smul_eq` (TD:308–316) requires genuine Holder and
symbol-growth/Lp hypotheses. `ae_eq_of_integral_contDiff_smul_eq`
(AEEqOfIntegralContDiff:195–199) identifies actual locally integrable representatives.
Current accepted modules supply the actual same-D localization and Sobolev facts;
their committed30ad6ddb normalized bytes match the working files below.
Earlier independent full code readings are reused only with these exact matches.

Density alone is not graph density. Pointwise bump-convolution convergence is
not L2 convergence; a direct mollifier route still needs actual L2 approximate
identity and weak-derivative/Laplacian commutation. A supplied Poincare/core
certificate or a tuple restating convergence premises does not produce this edge.
No claim that another suitable API is globally absent follows from this bounded
inspection. Source C2 potentials need not be C-infinity, so smoothing a potential
or silently differentiating it to arbitrary order would change the contract.

## Exposure and stop boundary

Fresh primary reads preceded the proposal. Exposure retained honestly: prior full
localization/Sobolev source and code reviews, own real-mixed/Schwartz source/API
prereads, and earlier covariance keywords/signatures/matching lines from bounded
BL searches. No ignored prototype, candidate log, anonymous reconstruction or
future mathematics verdict was read. No compiler ran. This note audits source
necessity and proposed interfaces only; it accepts no future production theorem.

Stop on changed D/u quantifiers, different limiting gradient, independent
sequences for each limit, missing common compact support, mere local or pointwise
convergence, unproved multiplier/domain adapters, or unsupported core/BL claims.
Each requires a precise repair or smaller producer with a separately recorded boundary.

